  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One of these per person",
      "items": [
        "Each stack is its own Compose project, lettuce-<name>, with its own tunnel, two Access applications and state directory.",
        "Only Gotenberg and the doc-tools volume are shared by every stack on the host, over one internal network per stack.",
        "Lettuce's host reaches only the BFF (app-server:8080); every garden page is on the garden host, and anything else there gets a 404."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Agents are root in the app-server and share its network namespace with the BFF; every container there drops NET_RAW.",
        "Garden services accept only the garden's Access application (CF_GARDEN_AUD), never Lettuce's JWT.",
        "The code editor runs nothing agents wrote; its terminals are SSH sessions into the shell, which is no stronger than an agent.",
        "Pipelock is advisory: the stack network keeps its direct route out.",
        "garden-news-radar fetches public websites directly, public addresses only (not drawn)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Volumes not drawn",
      "items": [
        "vault-data: only garden-vault. pipelock-data: only garden-pipelock. news-radar-data: only garden-news-radar.",
        "google-creds: the BFF, google-mcp, and garden-gmail-triggers read-only.",
        "code-server-sock, code-server-data, code-exec-keys: only the code editor's services.",
        "state/garden/gmail-triggers: only garden-gmail-triggers, outside every app-server mount."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Profiles",
      "items": [
        "garden-*: this repo's extras; garden starts with any garden page profile.",
        "search (searxng, ddg-mcp), google (google-mcp), cloudflared (required): upstream's.",
        "Not drawn: channel-gateway (upstream's telegram profile), which also shares the app-server's namespace."
      ]
    }
  ]
